{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/687519-elixirs","id":687519,"title":"Elixirs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-03T14:31:44-07:00","id":687519,"title":"Elixirs","content":"I'll admit I've never previously been a big fan of the Ascending Ones. They never really grabbed me flavor-wise. Recently though I've been giving them a reappraisal and finding some potential that I like. The main hurdle I'm still facing with them though is Elixirs. They seem expensive, punishing, and overall underpowered compared to other Endowments. Is there a hidden advantage or utility I'm not picking up from the text? Alternatively has anyone had any success in hacking the Elixir mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T03:35:40-07:00","id":688066,"title":"","content":"I take it you don't have Mortal remains, it's rules updates for elixirs is elixirs replenish between game sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T03:54:18-07:00","id":688104,"title":"","content":"Obviously you want to drop the costs drastically. The Elixir Merit costs exp but individual potions should not.<br /> <br /> Now the next thing to bear in mind is that the actual monster hunters in the Ascending Ones; they're not fighters they're assassins. Elixirs are a very specialised tool but an extreemly potent one when used correctly.<br /> <br /> An Assending one in a fight with a Vampire isn't in a far worse situation than an AKD with Relic weapons, a MM cell with combat Benedictions, in fact I think in a fight only Thaumatechnology is less useful. On the other hand, an Ascending One could just turn invisible walk into the Vampire's haven under the cover of sunlight and plant a bomb.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T20:25:57-07:00","id":690809,"title":"","content":"I do actually have Mortal Remains, but I'd missed that particular bit. Thank you, that is a very helpful update. <br /> <br /> I suppose my power concerns are mostly that the one and two dot Elixirs seem to have narrow utility and limited benefit for the high cost of using them. If you don't have to repurchase them after every use though, as in Mortal Remains, this is mitigated somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:26:33-07:00","id":700735,"title":"","content":"Well if you want to go further, since the AO are more potion users than actual alchemists, you could make the elixir rating just about having the resources to make or get a loan from another member then anything else. <br /> <br /> Going after vampires, stock up on stuff that should be helpful, carry different stuff when hunting werewolves the next week, and in between missions carry stuff that should help you get away from unspecified boogeymen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T22:00:43-07:00","id":733912,"title":"","content":"Here's a rules hack I'd like to suggest, inspired somewhat by the mechanics behind the Staff of Janus' Sabine Sacraments. The difference in this one, though, is that it's tied more to the Ascending One's status rather than dots in another Merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;A character begins play with a number of Elixirs whose total dot ratings equal her Elixir dots <i>multiplied</i> by her dots in Status (Ascending Ones). As the hunter rises in status, his growing reputation and extensive connections with others in the conspiracy increase his likelihood of being supplied with Elixirs to ensure his success on the Vigil&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}